# Database & Schema Safety Invariants

## 1. Additive-Only Schema Changes
- All changes to `prisma/schema.prisma` MUST be strictly **additive**: you may add new models, new fields, new enums, or new enum variants, but you may NEVER delete or rename an existing column, model, enum value, or relation.
- Dropping, renaming, or collapsing existing fields breaks backward compatibility with the deployed Neon PostgreSQL database and is strictly prohibited.
- New columns MUST be nullable or have a default value so existing deployed rows never block migration.

## 2. Protected Banking Fields (TeacherProfile)
- The following `TeacherProfile` banking/payout fields are **protected and MUST NOT be removed, renamed, or re-typed**:
  - `bankName` (String?)
  - `bankBranch` (String?)
  - `accountNumber` (String?)
  - `accountHolderName` (String?)
- Any diff that deletes one of these lines from `prisma/schema.prisma` fails the guardrail check.

## 3. LedgerEntryType Enum Immutability
- The `LedgerEntryType` enum must always contain exactly these 8 variants — adding is forbidden only in the sense of dropping; modifying or dropping any variant is strictly prohibited:
  - `CHARGE`
  - `PAYOUT`
  - `REFUND`
  - `PLATFORM_FEE`
  - `PENALTY`
  - `COMPENSATION`
  - `PLATFORM_COMPENSATION`
  - `ADJUSTMENT`
- Any diff that deletes or renames one of these variants fails the guardrail check.
- Financial records remain append-only: no `DELETE` behavior is allowed on `BillingLedger` / `TeacherPayout` code paths.

## 3. Migration Workflow (Non-Destructive)
- **NEVER** recommend or run `prisma migrate reset` (or `prisma migrate reset --force`) in any automated workflow — it destroys data and blocks against Neon.
- In development, when schema drift is detected, use **`npx prisma db push`** (non-destructive) to synchronize the schema, then reconcile a migration file via `prisma migrate dev` only when safe.
- Prefer a one-time `npx prisma migrate dev --name <feature>` for intentional additive changes; never drop-and-recreate.